Project: libjxl (the decoder, jxl_dec)
URL: https://github.com/libjxl/libjxl
Version: 0.13.0
License: BSD-3-Clause (see LICENSE; PATENTS: Google's patent grant)
Used for: JPEG XL decoding (stills and animations) in kit/intern/image (format_jxl.c).
          Blender reads JPEG XL through OpenImageIO, which uses libjxl.

Copied unmodified: lib/jxl (JPEGXL_INTERNAL_BASE_SOURCES and JPEGXL_INTERNAL_DEC_SOURCES of
lib/jxl_lists.cmake, and the headers they include: lib/jxl/cms/*.h, enc_ans_params.h,
jpeg/jpeg_data.h) and the public headers lib/include/jxl. Built as libjxl's jxl_dec without
boxes and JPEG reconstruction (JPEGXL_ENABLE_BOXES=0, JPEGXL_ENABLE_TRANSCODE_JPEG=0): so no
Brotli, which only those two need, and no CMS (skcms / lcms2): XYB images are asked for in
sRGB, which libjxl does without one. The Highway targets are libjxl's defaults
(HWY_DISABLED_TARGETS: what JPEGXL_HWY_TARGETS_OFF_BY_DEFAULT turns off).

BUI files (bui/jxl/):
  version.h      CMake writes it upstream from lib/jxl/version.h.in (0.13.0)
  jxl_export.h   CMake's generate_export_header writes it upstream; static: nothing exported
